WEBVTT


00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:06.210
Going to the extremes of racking,
this flat ribs stitch is amazing.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.760
With your ribber set to pitch H
arrange the needles like this.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.970
Notice all needles are and work
on the main bed and individual

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.040
needles are in work on the ribber.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.410
And these will create the zigzag.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.910
I've chosen to use every
fourth needle, but you can play

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.290
with different combinations.

00:00:29.175 --> 00:00:30.195
Think of it this way.

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:34.695
We're putting decorative traveling
knit stitches on the face of

00:00:34.695 --> 00:00:36.225
the purl side of the knitting.

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:42.165
Cast on with full needle rib,
then transfer the stitches

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:43.965
to your needle arrangement.

00:00:45.855 --> 00:00:49.955
You'll cast on with the ribber set to H0.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:01.309
When your cast on is complete, knit
one row from right to left, rack to H1.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.190
Knit from left to right.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:12.140
Rack to H2.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.500
Knit from right to left.

00:01:19.559 --> 00:01:22.320
To H3 knit from left to right.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:47.520
You'll be racking to an even
number and then you'll knit left.

00:01:48.225 --> 00:01:51.885
You'll rack to an odd number
and you'll knit right.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:17.250
To complete the zigzag, continue
racking all the way to 10 and then

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:23.060
work your way back to zero and repeat
for the length of your knitting.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:18.500
The secret of this stitch
pattern is the needle arrangement

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.100
and the extreme racking.

